:"allergen_source","summary":"Official menu descriptions support only narrow milk positives for explicitly named dairy products. They do not support complete allergen arrays, negatives, may-contain values, or cross-contact conclusions; the homepage's general kosher-packaging statement is not an item-level cross-contact disclosure.","sourceEvidenceIds":["terra-home","terra-menu"],"affectedAuditItemKeys":["6:sides-and-fries"]},{"findingId":"terra-missed-catering-surface-and-unresolved-third-party-product","severity":"medium","kind":"scope","summary":"Luna omitted the official catering surface and its restaurant-linked external catalog. Luna also referenced Vegan Pizza and Take & Bake Pizza on DoorDash without current-product records; Vegan Pizza is corroborated by the partial live DoorDash page, while Take & Bake Pizza could not be re-verified.","sourceEvidenceIds":["terra-catering","terra-catering-catalog","terra-doordash"],"affectedAuditItemKeys":[]}],"summary":"Ben Yehuda Pizza's Silver Spring identity and complete restaurant-issued all-day menu are verified. The frozen nine-row baseline is a failed extraction comprised entirely of non-product source material, while the official menu enumerates 29 real products. The catering service surface was missed and its linked catalog remains inaccessible. Explicit named dairy supports narrow restaurant-issued milk positives only; allergen completeness, negatives, may-contain, and cross-contact are unavailable. The effective result is discrepancy_found.","coordinatorNotes":["Escalate to Sol: the frozen catalog requires parser/extraction repair before a valid product-level reconciliation is possible.","Retain restaurant-issued milk positives only where the official menu explicitly names dairy; do not infer other allergens, negatives, or cross-contact.","Preserve ordering and catering evidence as restaurant-linked vendor evidence and DoorDash as third-party evidence."]}